# std::arch: the portable intrinsics, on every target (compiler/arch/README.md
# gives the columns). A `bits.*` form has a body, std's function of the
# same count, which a target without the instruction calls.
#
# name | features | signature | form | instruction | flags | memory | fold | semantics | equivalent | doc

count_ones | - | (x: u64) -> i64 | bits.ones | - | pure | none | bits.ones | r = the number of 1 bits of x | aarch64: cnt + addv; x86_64: popcnt (popcnt) | the number of 1 bits of x (std::count_ones)
has | - | (feature: [u8]) -> bool | feat.has | - | pure | none | feat | r = whether `feature` is known at this point (baseline, declared, guarded) | - | a constant: true when the feature is known where it is asked (never for another architecture's)
detect | - | (feature: [u8]) -> bool | feat.detect | - | pure | none | feat | r = whether the CPU running the program has `feature` | - | true when the running CPU has the feature: a constant when known or foreign, else one cached bit test
